come. Ralph turned to him. You're no good on a job like this. All the same.

414
00:25:11,119 --> 00:25:13,200
We don't want you, said Jack flatly.

415
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:15,759
Thre's enough. Piggy's glasses flashed.

416
00:25:15,759 --> 00:25:17,278
I was with him when he found the conchk.

417
00:25:17,278 --> 00:25:19,278
I was with him before anyone else was.

418
00:25:19,278 --> 00:25:20,798
Jack and the others paid no attention.

419
00:25:20,798 --> 00:25:24,319
There was a general dispersal. Ralph, Jack, and Simon jumped off the platform

420
00:25:24,319 --> 00:25:27,679
and walked along the sand past the bathing pool. Piggy hung bumbling behind

421
00:25:27,679 --> 00:25:30,480
them. "If Simon walks in the middle of us," said Ralph, "Then we could talk

422
00:25:30,480 --> 00:25:33,839
over his head." The three of them fell into step. This meant that every now and

423
00:25:33,839 --> 00:25:36,960
then Simon had to do a double shuffle to catch up with the others. Presently,

424
00:25:36,960 --> 00:25:39,000
Ralph stopped and turned back to Piggy.

425
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:43,278
"Look." Jack and Simon pretended to notice nothing. They walked on. "You

426
00:25:43,278 --> 00:25:47,599
can't come." Piggy's glasses were missed again, this time with humiliation. "You

427
00:25:47,599 --> 00:25:52,079
told him after what I said." His face flushed, his mouth trembled. "After I

428
00:25:52,079 --> 00:25:56,720
said I didn't want What on earth are you talking about? About being called Piggy?

429
00:25:56,720 --> 00:26:00,119
I said I didn't care as long as they didn't call me

430
00:26:00,119 --> 00:26:04,558
Piggy." And I said not to tell. And then you went and said straight out.

431
00:26:04,558 --> 00:26:07,278
Stillness descended on them. Ralph, looking with more understanding at

432
00:26:07,278 --> 00:26:09,278
Piggy, saw that he was hurt and crushed.

433
00:26:09,278 --> 00:26:13,599
He hovered between the two courses of apology or further insult. "Better Piggy

434
00:26:13,599 --> 00:26:17,038
than Fatty," he said at last, with the directness of genuine leadership. "And

435
00:26:17,038 --> 00:26:18,798
anyway, I'm sorry if you feel like that.

436
00:26:18,798 --> 00:26:20,480
Now go back, Piggy, and take names.

437
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:24,319
That's your job. So long." He turned and raced after the other two. Piggy stood,

438
00:26:24,319 --> 00:26:27,759
and the rose of indignation faded slowly from his cheeks. He went back to the

439
00:26:27,759 --> 00:26:31,519
platform. The three boys walked briskly on the sand. The tide was low, and there

440
00:26:31,519 --> 00:26:34,720
was a strip of weedstrun beach that was almost as firm as a road. A kind of

441
00:26:34,720 --> 00:26:37,359
glamour was spread over them and the scene, and they were conscious of the

442
00:26:37,359 --> 00:26:40,558
glamour and made happy by it. They turned to each other laughing excitedly,

443
00:26:40,558 --> 00:26:44,319
talking, not listening. The air was bright. Ralph, faced by the task of

444
00:26:44,319 --> 00:26:46,880
translating all this into an explanation, stood on his head and fell

445
00:26:46,880 --> 00:26:51,038
over. When they had done laughing, Simon stroked Ralph's arm shily, and they had

446
00:26:51,038 --> 00:26:55,359
to laugh again. "Come on," said Jack presently. "We're explorers. Well

447
00:26:55,359 --> 00:26:58,079
go to the end of the island," said Ralph, "and look around the corner. If

448
00:26:58,079 --> 00:27:01,839
it is an island now toward the end of the afternoon, the mirages were settling

449
00:27:01,839 --> 00:27:04,880
a little. They found the end of the island quite distinct and not magicked

450
00:27:04,880 --> 00:27:08,159
out of shape or sense. There was a jumble of the usual squareness with one

451
00:27:08,159 --> 00:27:09,839
great block sitting out in the lagoon.

452
00:27:09,839 --> 00:27:14,400
Seabirds were nesting there. Like icing, said Ralph on a pink cake. We shan see

453
00:27:14,400 --> 00:27:17,759
around this corner, said Jack, because there isn't one, only a slow curve. And

454
00:27:17,759 --> 00:27:21,278
you can see the rocks get worse. Ralph shaded his eyes and followed the jagged

455
00:27:21,278 --> 00:27:24,000
outline of the crags up toward the mountain. This part of the beach was

456
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:27,278
nearer the mountain than any other that they had seen. We'll try climbing the

457
00:27:27,278 --> 00:27:30,319
mountain from here, he said. I should think this is the easiest way. There's

458
00:27:30,319 --> 00:27:34,000
less of that jungly stuff and more pink rock. Come on. The three boys began to

459
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:37,278
scramble up. Some unknown force had wrenched and shattered these cubes so

460
00:27:37,278 --> 00:27:43,200
that they lay a skew, often piled diminishingly on each other. The most usual feature of the

461
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:46,880
rock was a pink cliff surmounted by a skewed block, and that again surmounted,

462
00:27:46,880 --> 00:27:50,159
and that again, till the pigness became a stack of balanced rock projecting

463
00:27:50,159 --> 00:27:53,679
through the looped fantasy of the forest creepers. Where the pink cliffs rose out

464
00:27:53,679 --> 00:27:57,278
of the ground, there were often narrow tracks winding upwards. They could edge

465
00:27:57,278 --> 00:28:00,720
along them deep in the plant world, their faces to the rock. What made this

466
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:04,159
track? Jack paused, wiping the sweat from his face. Ralph stood by him,

467
00:28:04,159 --> 00:28:06,640
breathless. Men. Jack shook his head.

468
00:28:06,640 --> 00:28:10,319
Animals. Ralph peered into the darkness under the trees. The forest minutely

469
00:28:10,319 --> 00:28:13,519
vibrated. Come on. The difficulty was not the steep ascent around the

470
00:28:13,519 --> 00:28:16,240
shoulders of rock, but the occasional plunges through the undergrowth to get

471
00:28:16,240 --> 00:28:19,440
to the next path. Here the roots and stems of creepers were in such tangles

472
00:28:19,440 --> 00:28:22,798
that the boys had to thread through them like pliant needles. Their only guide,

473
00:28:22,798 --> 00:28:25,359
apart from the brown ground and occasional flashes of light through the

474
00:28:25,359 --> 00:28:27,359
foliage, was the tendency of slope.

475
00:28:27,359 --> 00:28:30,720
Whether this hole, laced as it was with the cables of creepers, stood higher

476
00:28:30,720 --> 00:28:33,440
than that. Somehow they moved up.

477
00:28:33,440 --> 00:28:36,319
Immured in these tangles, at perhaps their most difficult moment, Ralph

478
00:28:36,319 --> 00:28:38,440
turned with shining eyes to the others.

479
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:43,440
Wacko, wizard, smashing. The cause of their pleasure was not obvious. All

480
00:28:43,440 --> 00:28:45,359
three were hot, dirty, and exhausted.

481
00:28:45,359 --> 00:28:48,640
Ralph was badly scratched. The creepers were as thick as their thighs and left

482
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:51,440
little but tunnels for further penetration. Ralph shouted

483
00:28:51,440 --> 00:28:55,119
experimentally, and they listened to the muted echoes. "This is real exploring,"

484
00:28:55,119 --> 00:28:59,278
said Jack. "I bet nobody's been here before." "We ought to draw a map," said

485
00:28:59,278 --> 00:29:00,960
Ralph, "Only we haven't done any paper."

486
00:29:00,960 --> 00:29:05,038
"We can make scratches on bark," said Simon, "and rub black stuff in." Again

487
00:29:05,038 --> 00:29:09,960
came the solemn communion of shining eyes in the gloom. "Wacko

488
00:29:09,960 --> 00:29:13,519
wizard!" There was no place for standing on one's head. This time, Ralph

489
00:29:13,519 --> 00:29:16,640
expressed the intensity of his emotion by pretending to knock Simon down, and

490
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:19,839
soon they were a happy heaving pile in the underdusk. When they had fallen

491
00:29:19,839 --> 00:29:22,240
apart, Ralph spoke first. Got to get on.

492
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:25,200
The pink granite of the next cliff was further back from the creepers and trees

493
00:29:25,200 --> 00:29:26,720
so that they could trot up the path.

494
00:29:26,720 --> 00:29:30,000
This again led into more forest so that they had a glimpse of the spread sea.

495
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:33,519
With openness came the sun. It dried the sweat that had soaked their clothes in

496
00:29:33,519 --> 00:29:37,359
the dark, damp heat. At last the way to the top looked like a scramble over pink

497
00:29:37,359 --> 00:29:40,640
rock. With no more plunging through darkness, the boys chose their way

498
00:29:40,640 --> 00:29:45,200
through defiles and over heaps of sharp stone. Look, look. High over this end of

499
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:48,640
the island, the shattered rocks lifted up their stacks and chimneys. This one,

500
00:29:48,640 --> 00:29:52,960
against which Jack leaned, moved with a grading sound when they pushed. Come on.

501
00:29:52,960 --> 00:29:56,159
But not come on to the top. The assault on the summit must wait while the three

502
00:29:56,159 --> 00:29:59,919
boys accepted this challenge. The rock was as large as a small motor car.

503
00:29:59,919 --> 00:30:04,480
Heave. Sway back and forth. Catch the rhythm. Heave. Increase the swing of the

504
00:30:04,480 --> 00:30:08,159
pendulum. Increase. Increase. Come up and bear against that point of furthest

505
00:30:08,159 --> 00:30:13,278
balance. Increase. Increase. Heave. The great rock loitered poised on one toe.

506
00:30:13,278 --> 00:30:18,159
Decided not to return. Moved through the air. Fell. Struck. turned over, leapt,

507
00:30:18,159 --> 00:30:21,919
droning through the air, and smashed a deep hole in the canopy of the forest.

508
00:30:21,919 --> 00:30:26,159
Echoes and birds flew. White and pink dust floated. The forest, further down,

509
00:30:26,159 --> 00:30:30,359
shook as with the passage of an enraged monster. And then the island was still

510
00:30:30,359 --> 00:30:33,640
wacko, like a bomb.

511
00:30:33,640 --> 00:30:37,759
Weeoo! Not for 5 minutes could they drag themselves away from this triumph, but

512
00:30:37,759 --> 00:30:41,278
they left at last. The way to the top was easy after that. As they reached the

513
00:30:41,278 --> 00:30:47,000
last stretch, Ralph stopped. Golly! They were on the lip of a circular

514
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:51,440
hollow in the side of the mountain. This was filled with a blue flower, a rock

515
00:30:51,440 --> 00:30:54,798
plant of some sort, and the overflow hung down the vent and spilled lavishly

516
00:30:54,798 --> 00:30:58,558
among the canopy of the forest. The air was thick with butterflies, lifting,

517
00:30:58,558 --> 00:31:02,079
fluttering, settling. Beyond the hollow was the square top of the mountain, and

518
00:31:02,079 --> 00:31:05,519
soon they were standing on it. They had guessed before that this was an island,

519
00:31:05,519 --> 00:31:08,319
clambering among the pink rocks, with the sea on either side and the crystal

520
00:31:08,319 --> 00:31:12,079
heights of air. They had known by some instinct that the sea lay on every side.

521
00:31:12,079 --> 00:31:15,038
But there seemed something more fitting in leaving the last word till they stood

522
00:31:15,038 --> 00:31:18,640
on the top and could see a circular horizon of water. Ralph turned to the

523
00:31:18,640 --> 00:31:23,278
others. This belongs to us. It was roughly boat-shaped, humped near this

524
00:31:23,278 --> 00:31:26,319
end, with behind them the jumbled descent to the shore. On either side

525
00:31:26,319 --> 00:31:30,079
rocks, cliffs, treetops, and a steep slope. Forward there the length of the

526
00:31:30,079 --> 00:31:34,240
boat, a tamer descent, treeclad with hints of pink, and then the jungly flat

527
00:31:34,240 --> 00:31:38,319
of the island, dense green, but drawn at the end to a pink tail. There, where the

528
00:31:38,319 --> 00:31:42,319
island petered out in water, was another island, a rock, almost detached,

529
00:31:42,319 --> 00:31:46,558
standing like a fort, facing them across the green with one bold pink bastion.

530
00:31:46,558 --> 00:31:50,240
The boys surveyed all this, then looked out to see. They were high up, and the

531
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:54,398
afternoon had advanced. The view was not robbed of sharpness by mirage. That's a

532
00:31:54,398 --> 00:31:58,159
reef, a coral reef. I've seen pictures like that. The reef enclosed more than

533
00:31:58,159 --> 00:32:01,119
one side of the island, lying perhaps a mile out, and parallel to what they now

534
00:32:01,119 --> 00:32:04,558
thought of as their beach. The coral was scribbled in the sea as though a giant

535
00:32:04,558 --> 00:32:08,079
had bent down to reproduce the shape of the island in a flowing chalk line, but

536
00:32:08,079 --> 00:32:13,119
tired before he had finished. Inside was peacock water, rocks and weeds showing

537
00:32:13,119 --> 00:32:17,759
as in an aquarium. Outside was the dark blue of the sea. The tide was running so

538
00:32:17,759 --> 00:32:20,720
that long streaks of foam tailed away from the reef, and for a moment they

539
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:24,640
felt that the boat was moving steadily a stern. Jack pointed down. That's where

540
00:32:24,640 --> 00:32:28,798
we landed. Beyond falls and cliffs there was a gash visible in the trees. There

541
00:32:28,798 --> 00:32:32,558
were the splintered trunks and then the drag, leaving only a fringe of palm

542
00:32:32,558 --> 00:32:37,240
between the scar and the sea. There, too, jutting into the lagoon, was the

543
00:32:37,240 --> 00:32:41,919
platform, with insect-like figures moving near it. Ralph sketched a twining

544
00:32:41,919 --> 00:32:45,200
line from the bald spot on which they stood, down a slope, a gully through

545
00:32:45,200 --> 00:32:48,319
flowers, round and down to the rock where the scar started. That's the

546
00:32:48,319 --> 00:32:52,640
quickest way back. Eyes shining, mouths open, triumphant, they savored the right

547
00:32:52,640 --> 00:32:54,880
of domination. They were lifted up.

548
00:32:54,880 --> 00:32:59,519
We're friends. There's no village smoke and no boats, said Ralph wisely. We'll

549
00:32:59,519 --> 00:33:03,200
make sure later, but I think it's uninhabited. We'll get food, cried Jack.

550
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:05,919
Hunt, catch things until they fetch us.

551
00:33:05,919 --> 00:33:09,038
Simon looked at them both, saying nothing but nodding till his black hair

552
00:33:09,038 --> 00:33:13,200
flopped backwards and forwards. His face was glowing. Ralph looked down the other

553
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:17,839
way where there was no reef. Steeper, said Jack. Ralph made a cupping gesture.

554
00:33:17,839 --> 00:33:21,839
That bit of forest down there. The mountain holds it up. Every point of the

555
00:33:21,839 --> 00:33:26,398
mountain held up trees, flowers, and trees. Now the forest stirred, roared,

556
00:33:26,398 --> 00:33:29,759
flailed. The nearer acres of rock flowers fluttered, and for a half a

557
00:33:29,759 --> 00:33:33,839
minute the breeze blew cool on their faces. Ralph spread his arms. "All

558
00:33:33,839 --> 00:33:38,000
ours!" They laughed and tumbled and shouted on the mountain. "I'm hungry."

559
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:41,038
When Simon mentioned his hunger, the others became aware of theirs. "Come

560
00:33:41,038 --> 00:33:44,240
on," said Ralph. "We found out what we wanted to know." They scrambled down a

561
00:33:44,240 --> 00:33:48,000
rock slope, dropped among flowers, and made their way under the trees. Here

562
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:51,599
they paused and examined the bushes around them curiously. Simon spoke

563
00:33:51,599 --> 00:33:54,319
first. "Like candles! Candle bushes.

564
00:33:54,319 --> 00:33:58,079
Candle buds. The bushes were dark evergreen and aromatic, and the many

565
00:33:58,079 --> 00:34:01,679
buds were wax and green and folded up against the light. Jack slashed at one

566
00:34:01,679 --> 00:34:05,358
with his knife, and the scent spilled over them. Candle buds? You couldn't

567
00:34:05,358 --> 00:34:10,639
light them, said Ralph. They just look like candles. Green candles, said Jack

568
00:34:10,639 --> 00:34:14,320
contemptuously. We can't eat them. Come on. They were in the beginnings of the

569
00:34:14,320 --> 00:34:18,079
thick forest, plonking with weary feet on a track, when they heard the noises,

570
00:34:18,079 --> 00:34:21,679
squeaking, and the hard strike of hoofs on a path. As they pushed forward, the

571
00:34:21,679 --> 00:34:24,960
squeaking increased till it became a frenzy. They found a piglet caught in a

572
00:34:24,960 --> 00:34:28,639
curtain of creepers, throwing itself at the elastic traces in all the madness of

573
00:34:28,639 --> 00:34:32,639
extreme terror. Its voice was thin, needle sharp, and insistent. The three

574
00:34:32,639 --> 00:34:35,918
boys rushed forward, and Jack drew his knife again with a flourish. He raised

575
00:34:35,918 --> 00:34:39,918
his arm in the air. There came a pause, a hiatus. The pig continued to scream

576
00:34:39,918 --> 00:34:43,519
and the creepers to jerk, and the blade continued to flash at the end of a bony

577
00:34:43,519 --> 00:34:47,119
arm. The pause was only long enough for them to understand what an enormity the

578
00:34:47,119 --> 00:34:50,639
downward stroke would be. Then the piglet tore loose from the creepers and

579
00:34:50,639 --> 00:34:53,760
scured into the undergrowth. They were left looking at each other and the place

580
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:58,719
of terror. Jack's face was white under the freckles. He noticed that he still held

581
00:34:58,719 --> 00:35:02,159
the knife aloft and brought his arm down, replacing the blade in the sheath.

582
00:35:02,159 --> 00:35:06,000
Then they all three laughed ashamedly and began to climb back to the track. I

583
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:09,920
was choosing a place, said Jack. I was just waiting for a moment to decide

584
00:35:09,920 --> 00:35:14,239
where to stab him. You should stick a pig, said Ralph fiercely. They always

585
00:35:14,239 --> 00:35:17,760
talk about sticking a pig. You cut a pig's throat to let the blood out, said

586
00:35:17,760 --> 00:35:20,000
Jack. Otherwise, you can't eat the meat.

587
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:24,320
Why didn't you? They knew very well why he hadn't. Because of the enormity of

588
00:35:24,320 --> 00:35:28,239
the knife descending and cutting into living flesh. Because of the unbearable

589
00:35:28,239 --> 00:35:32,480
blood. I was going to, said Jack. He was ahead of them, and they could not see

590
00:35:32,480 --> 00:35:37,280
his face. I was choosing a place. Next time. He snatched his knife out of the

591
00:35:37,280 --> 00:35:39,358
sheath and slammed it into a tree trunk.

592
00:35:39,358 --> 00:35:43,199
Next time there would be no mercy. He looked round fiercely, daring them to

593
00:35:43,199 --> 00:35:46,639
contradict. Then they broke out into the sunlight, and for a while they were busy

594
00:35:46,639 --> 00:35:52,480
finding and devouring food as they moved down the scar toward the platform and the

595
00:35:53,239 --> 00:35:55,000
meeting. Lord of the Flies.
